+// ---------- Float4 kernel with halo register reuse ----------
+// Each thread processes consecutive groups: gid, gid+bs, gid+2*bs, ...
+// Within a single iteration, process the group with float4 load.
+// Across iterations, reuse previous group's tail as halo.
+// But since stride = bs (typically 32-256), consecutive loop iterations
+// are NOT adjacent in memory (gap = bs*4 elements). So halo reuse only
+// works if we process ADJACENT groups. We restructure: each thread handles
+// a contiguous chunk of ceil(groups/bs) groups starting at tid*chunk_size.
